{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 393018, "name": "Piotr Dobrogost", "username": "piotr-dobrogost", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/piotr-dobrogost/{size}/39995_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-02T22:01:28.121Z", "cooked": "<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">[miner@hostx ~]$ sudo dnf remove openh264\n(…)\nTransaction Summary:\n Removing:         441 packages\n\nAfter this operation, 3 GiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 3 GiB).\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-02T22:01:28.121Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 415, "reads": 46, "readers_count": 45, "score": 2089.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Piotr Dobrogost", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 21886, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393021, "name": "One", "username": "einer", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-04-02T22:14:21.159Z", "cooked": "<p>… it’s basically saying that all those packages depend on openh264 … so, if you remove openh264, may as well remove those that depend on it as well …</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-02T22:14:21.159Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 47, "readers_count": 46, "score": 34.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "One", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 23724, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393025, "name": "Timothée Ravier", "username": "siosm", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/siosm/{size}/79_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-02T22:29:31.435Z", "cooked": "<p>If you don’t want to use <code>openh264</code> then you have to swap it with <code>noopenh264</code> with <code>dnf swap</code> and then lock the package so that it does not get replaced again with <code>dnf version lock</code> or something similar.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-02T22:29:31.435Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 49, "readers_count": 48, "score": 44.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Timothée Ravier", "primary_group_name": "packager", "flair_name": "packager", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 68, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Fedora Engineering Steering Committee", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 90, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/3", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393054, "name": "Lars", "username": "l-c-g", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/l-c-g/{size}/36557_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-03T06:09:23.204Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"einer\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"148134\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/f5a326/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> One:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>… it’s basically saying that all those packages depend on openh264</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not <strong>all</strong> of them depend on OpenH264.</p>\n<p>When you remove a package, the dependency resolver has to do two things:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>walk up the dependency tree and remove all packages whose dependencies are no longer fulfilled.</li>\n<li>remove all child packages that were automatically installed as a dependency of the removed package(s).</li>\n</ol>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"piotr-dobrogost\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"148134\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/piotr-dobrogost/48/39995_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Piotr Dobrogost:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">[miner@hostx ~]$ sudo dnf remove openh264\n(…)\nTransaction Summary:\n Removing:         441 packages\n\nAfter this operation, 3 GiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 3 GiB).\n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You can find which (installed) packages have a specific dependency with <code>dnf repoquery --whatrequires</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">~ ❯ dnf repoquery --installed --whatrequires openh264\nffmpeg-libs-0:7.1.1-3.fc41.x86_64\nfreerdp-libs-2:3.12.0-1.fc41.x86_64\nfreerdp2-libs-0:2.11.7-5.fc41.x86_64\ngstreamer1-plugin-openh264-0:1.24.11-1.fc41.x86_64\nlibheif-0:1.19.7-1.fc41.x86_64\nmozilla-openh264-0:2.4.1-2.fc41.x86_64\nqt6-qtwebengine-0:6.8.2-4.fc41.x86_64\n</code></pre>\n<p>So, if I tried to remove <code>openh264</code> from my (<em>KDE, not Fedora Workstation</em>) system, as a first step the seven packages that directly depend on <code>openh264</code> would need to be removed as their <code>openh264</code> dependency is no longer fulfilled.</p>\n<p>Next, all packages that depend on one of these seven would have have to be removed. For example, for <code>ffmpeg-libs</code> on my system, the following packages depend on that and would need to be removed:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">~ ❯ dnf repoquery --installed --whatrequires ffmpeg-libs\nffmpeg-0:7.1.1-3.fc41.x86_64\nffmpegthumbs-0:24.12.3-1.fc41.x86_64\ngstreamer1-plugin-libav-0:1.24.11-1.fc41.x86_64\nkf6-kfilemetadata-0:6.12.0-1.fc41.x86_64\nkpipewire-0:6.3.3-1.fc41.x86_64\nlibavdevice-0:7.1.1-3.fc41.x86_64\nlibchromaprint-0:1.5.1-24.fc41.x86_64\nlibheif-freeworld-0:1.19.7-1.fc41.x86_64\nqt6-qtmultimedia-0:6.8.2-1.fc41.x86_64\nqt6-qtwebengine-0:6.8.2-4.fc41.x86_64\n</code></pre>\n<p>This continues until the resolver has reached a stable configuration or an error. On your system, this means removing an additional 440 packages when removing <code>openh264</code>.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-03T07:52:17.986Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 2, "incoming_link_count": 24, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 148.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Lars", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 23724, "username": "einer", "name": "One", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/e/f5a326/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 20111, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393071, "name": "Piotr Dobrogost", "username": "piotr-dobrogost", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/piotr-dobrogost/{size}/39995_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-03T08:56:27.603Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for all the information.<br>\nThe problem with the list was that there were packages there having nothing to do with h264 like for example <code>openvpn</code> or <code>kate</code> (KDE text editor) and many others which intuitively should not be connected with <code>openh264</code> neither directly nor indirectly in the dependency tree. That seemed like some problem with the package database.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-03T09:45:50.397Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 8, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 46.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Piotr Dobrogost", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 20111, "username": "l-c-g", "name": "Lars", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/l-c-g/{size}/36557_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 21886, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393079, "name": "Leigh Scott", "username": "leigh123linux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-03T09:27:48.558Z", "cooked": "<p>Nothing directly depends openh264, everything in the repo’s is built using noopenh264</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">$ dnf repoquery --whatrequires noopenh264\nUpdating and loading repositories:\nRepositories loaded.\nchromium-0:134.0.6998.165-1.fc42.x86_64\nffmpeg-libs-0:7.1.1-3.fc42.x86_64\nfreerdp-libs-2:3.12.0-1.fc42.i686\nfreerdp-libs-2:3.12.0-1.fc42.x86_64\nfreerdp2-libs-0:2.11.7-7.fc42.i686\nfreerdp2-libs-0:2.11.7-7.fc42.x86_64\ngstreamer1-plugin-openh264-0:1.26.0-1.fc42.i686\ngstreamer1-plugin-openh264-0:1.26.0-1.fc42.x86_64\nlibavcodec-free-0:7.1.1-3.fc42.i686\nlibavcodec-free-0:7.1.1-3.fc42.x86_64\nlibavcodec-freeworld-0:7.1.1-3.fc42.x86_64\nlibheif-0:1.19.7-1.fc42.i686\nlibheif-0:1.19.7-1.fc42.x86_64\nmozilla-openh264-0:2.4.1-2.fc42.x86_64\nnoopenh264-devel-0:2.5.0-2.fc42.i686\nnoopenh264-devel-0:2.5.0-2.fc42.x86_64\nopenh264-devel-0:2.4.1-2.fc42.x86_64\nqt6-qtwebengine-0:6.8.2-4.fc42.x86_64\ntelegram-desktop-0:5.12.3-1.fc42.x86_64\ntelegram-desktop-0:5.13.1-1.fc42.x86_64\nxpra-codecs-freeworld-0:5.0.10-3.fc42.x86_64\nxrdp-1:0.10.2-11.fc42.i686\nxrdp-1:0.10.2-11.fc42.x86_64\n</code></pre>\n<p>To switch is easy</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf swap *\\openh264\\*  noopenh264\n</code></pre>\n<p>And to prevent it being installed again</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf config-manager setopt  fedora-cisco-openh264.enabled=0\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-03T09:37:34.094Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 584, "reads": 29, "readers_count": 28, "score": 2955.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Leigh Scott", "primary_group_name": "packager", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packager Sponsor", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10536, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}, {"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393080, "name": "Piotr Dobrogost", "username": "piotr-dobrogost", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/piotr-dobrogost/{size}/39995_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-03T09:37:54.998Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for sharing <code>sudo dnf swap \\*openh264\\*  noopenh264</code> as it looks like the stars are essential here.</p>\n<p>No stars (notice <code>Problem</code> note and <code>openh264</code> replacing itself?!):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf swap openh264 noopenh264    \nUpdating and loading repositories:\nRepositories loaded.\nProblem: cannot install the best candidate for the job\n  - conflicting requests\n\nPackage                        Arch    Version                         Repository                   Size\nReinstalling:\n openh264                      x86_64  2.4.1-2.fc41                    fedora-cisco-openh264     1.1 MiB\n   replacing openh264          x86_64  2.4.1-2.fc41                    &lt;unknown&gt;                 1.1 MiB\n\nTransaction Summary:\n Reinstalling:       1 package\n Replacing:          1 package\n\nTotal size of inbound packages is 420 KiB. Need to download 420 KiB.\nAfter this operation, 0 B extra will be used (install 1 MiB, remove 1 MiB).\nIs this ok [y/N]:\n</code></pre>\n<p>With stars (looks OK):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf swap \\*openh264\\* noopenh264\nUpdating and loading repositories:\nRepositories loaded.\nProblem: cannot install the best candidate for the job\n  - conflicting requests\n\nPackage                           Arch      Version                           Repository            Size\nRemoving:\n gstreamer1-plugin-openh264       x86_64    1.24.11-1.fc41                    updates           70.9 KiB\n mozilla-openh264                 x86_64    2.4.1-2.fc41                      &lt;unknown&gt;          1.1 MiB\n openh264                         x86_64    2.4.1-2.fc41                      &lt;unknown&gt;          1.1 MiB\nInstalling:\n noopenh264                       x86_64    0.1.0~openh264_2.4.1-2.fc41       fedora            43.0 KiB\n\nTransaction Summary:\n Installing:         1 package\n Removing:           3 packages\n\nTotal size of inbound packages is 22 KiB. Need to download 22 KiB.\nAfter this operation, 2 MiB will be freed (install 43 KiB, remove 2 MiB).\nIs this ok [y/N]:\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-03T09:37:54.998Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 23, "reads": 27, "readers_count": 26, "score": 125.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Piotr Dobrogost", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 10536, "username": "leigh123linux", "name": "Leigh Scott", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 21886, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 393081, "name": "Leigh Scott", "username": "leigh123linux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/leigh123linux/{size}/45562_2.png", "created_at": "2025-04-03T09:39:31.598Z", "cooked": "<p>Don’t forget to disable cisco repo after removing their packages</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf config-manager setopt  fedora-cisco-openh264.enabled=0\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2025-04-03T09:39:31.598Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 7, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 16, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 100.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 148134, "topic_slug": "why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository", "display_username": "Leigh Scott", "primary_group_name": "packager", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packager Sponsor", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 21886, "username": "piotr-dobrogost", "name": "Piotr Dobrogost", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/piotr-dobrogost/{size}/39995_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 10536, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/why-does-dnf-want-to-remove-441-packages-when-removing-openh264-installed-from-fedora-cisco-openh264-repository/148134/8", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_us